tiate meloxicam fifteen milligrams once a day\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and i would encourage you to use a pillow to rest your arm on and you may also ice the area\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] for your epilepsy you\'ve been doing well on keppra and you deny any recent seizures so continue keppra five hundred milligrams twice a day i\'ll go ahead and refill that for you\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and for your depression you\'re doing well with therapy so i\'m going to initiate lexapro ten milligrams once a day\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] and for your peptic ulcer disease your recent endoscopy revealed gastritis so continue protonix forty milligrams once daily before meals\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] any questions for me\n[patient] nope i\'m good\n[doctor] okay great thanks for coming in today\n[patient] thanks }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi, anna. how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing alright. how about you?\n[doctor] i\'m doing well. so, i know that the nurse told you about dax. i\'d like to tell dax a little bit about you. hey, dragon, i\'m seeing a patient here, anna, and she\'s a 26-year-old female. she\'s got a past medical history of epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease. and she\'s coming in today because she\'s got some joint pain.\n[patient] yes, my left elbow has really been bothering me.\n[doctor] okay. so, tell me a little bit about what\'s going on with your elbow. what\'s been going on?\n[patient] well, i sit at a desk all day for work and my elbows are always bent. and then after work, it\'s really hard for me to flex and extend my left elbow. it\'s been really stiff and painful. and i\'ve noticed some swelling on the back of my elbow, my olecranon. i\'m right-handed, so i can still write, which is great. but typing is really difficult. i don\'t have any numbness or tingling in my hands, but i do have some weakness in my arm, but nothing too significant. and i don\'t have any fever or chills.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any recent se