g all of her immunosuppression medication.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\n• Cardiovascular: Denies chest pain or dyspnea on exertion.\n• Respiratory: Denies shortness of breath\n• Neurological: Endorses headaches.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAMINATION\n\n• Constitutional: in no apparent distress.\n• Neck: Supple without thyromegaly or lymphadenopathy.\n• Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. No wheezes, rales, or rhonchi.\n• Cardiovascular: 2/6 systolic ejection murmur.\n• Musculoskeletal: No edema.\n• Integumentary: Scar on left flank from kidney transplant, healed.\n\nRESULTS\n\nCreatinine: normal.\n\nElectrocardiogram: normal.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN\n\nMs. Susan Watson is a 26-year-old female who is here today for a high blood pressure check.\n\nHypertension.\n• Medical Reasoning: Her blood pressure is elevated today and based on her recent home monitoring.\n• Additional Testing: I would like to get a lipid panel and metabolic panel.\n• Medical Treatment: carvedilol 25 mg twice a day to help bring her blood pressure down.\n\nStatus post kidney transplant.\n• Medical Reasoning: Doing well.\nKidney function stable.\n• Medical Treatment: Continue current medications.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] hi susan, how are you today?\n[patient] i\'m doing well, doctor, just here for a high blood pressure check.\n[doctor] okay, so you\'re here for a high blood pressure check. how have you been feeling?\n[patient] i\'ve been feeling alright. i\'ve just noticed that my blood pressure has been a little high, especially recently.\n[doctor] okay, and what have you been doing to check your blood pressure at home?\n[patient] i\'ve been checking it with a monitor at home. it\'s been running around 150 over 90.\n[doctor] okay, that\'s a bit high. are you taking any medication for your high blood pressure?\n[patient] yes, i\'m taking norvasc 10 milligrams daily.\n[doctor] okay, and have you had any side effects from the norvasc?\n[patient] no, i\'ve not noticed any side effects.\n[doctor] okay, and have you had any other symptoms like chest pain or shortness of breath?\n[patient] no chest pain or shortness of breath.\n[doctor] any headaches?\n[patient] yes, i\'ve had some headaches, but i\'m not sure if it\'s from stress at work or the high blood pressure.\n[doctor] okay, well, we\'ll check that out. how about your kidney transplant? how\'s that going?\n[patient] it\'s going well. i\'m taking all of my immunosuppressive medications.\n[doctor] okay, good to hear. i\'m gon na go ahead and do a quick physical exam on you. i\'m gon na call out some of my findings as i go along. so, you\'re in no apparent distress. your neck is supple, no thyromegaly or lymphadenopathy. your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes, rales or rhonchi. your heart has a two over six systolic ejection murmur, but that\'s been present on previous exams. you have no edema. your scar on your left flank from the kidney transplant is healed and looks good. i\'m gon na go ahead and check your vitals. your blood pressure is 160 over 98. your heart rate is 76. your respiratory rate is 16. your temperature is 98.6, and your oxygen saturation is 98 % on room air. so, i\'m gon na go ahead and order a lipid panel and a metabolic panel to check your kidney function. i also reviewed your ecg that was done before you came in, and everything looks normal. so, for your high blood pressure, i\'d like to add carvedilol 25 milligrams twice a day. this will help bring your blood pressure down. i also recommend some diet changes, such as reducing your salt intake and increasing your intake of fruits and vegetables. do you have any questions about that?\n[patient] no, that sounds good.\n[doctor] okay, great. for your kidney transplant, continue with your current medications. i\'ll also go ahead and order a repeat kidney function panel. any other questions for me?\n[patient] no, that\'s it.\n[doctor] okay, great. i\'ll see you back in a month to check your blood pressure. if you have any questions or concerns before then, feel free to call the office.\n[patient] okay, thank you, doctor.\n[doctor] you\'re welcome. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi susan how are you today\n[patient] i\'m doing okay\n[doctor] good to hear that so i know the nurse mentioned you\'re here for a high blood pressure check so let\'s talk a little bit about that i see that you\'ve been struggling with high blood pressure for a while now and it\'s been running a little out of control lately can you tell me a little bit about that\n[patient] yeah i\'ve always had high blood pressure but it seems like it\'s gotten worse lately and i\'m just looking for some new medication or maybe some diet changes to help\n[doctor] okay and you\'re currently taking norvasc ten milligrams a day for your high blood pressure\n[patient] yes i am\n[doctor] and what\'s your blood pressure been running like at home\n[patient] it\'s been over one fifty\n[doctor] okay and have you been experiencing any headaches or anything like that\n[patient] i\'ve had some headaches but i\'m not sure if it\'s because of the stress at work or my high blood pressure\n[doctor] okay and have you had any chest pain or shortness of breath\n[patient] no i have not\n[doctor] okay and i know that you\'ve had a kidney transplant a few years ago how has everything been going with that\n[patient] everything has been going well\n[doctor] that\'s great to hear and you\'re taking all of your immunosuppression medication\n[patient] yes i am\n[doctor] okay well let\'s go ahead and do a quick physical exam so i know that you\'re in no apparent distress your neck is supple without thyromegaly or lymphadenopathy your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally no wheezes rales or rhonchi you have a two over six systolic ejection murmur on your heart exam and your abdominal exam is