rior lumbar fusion with hardware in good position.\n\nIMPRESSION\n\nLumbar spine strain.\n\nPLAN\n\nAt this point, I discussed the diagnosis and treatment options with the patient. I have recommended ice and heat. She will continue with Motrin 800 mg 3 times a day with food. She will follow up with me as needed.\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] hi ms. lee. how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing okay.\n[doctor] so, i see that you\'re here for back pain. can you tell me what happened?\n[patient] yeah, so i was at a birthday party and i ran into the railing of the staircase and twisted my back.\n[doctor] okay. and did you fall or just hit into it?\n[patient] i just hit into it.\n[doctor] okay. and have you experienced anything like this before?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and are you having any pain radiating down your legs?\n[patient] no, just in my back.\n[doctor] okay. and does it hurt when you lie flat?\n[patient] yes, it does.\n[doctor] okay. and twisting motions?\n[patient] yes, twisting motions make it worse.\n[doctor] okay. are you taking any medications?\n[patient] just ibuprofen.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical conditions?\n[patient] i have anxiety.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any surgeries in the past?\n[patient] yes, i had a lumbar fusion.\n[doctor] okay. and how long ago was that?\n[patient] it was a few years ago.\n[doctor] okay. and are you taking any other medications?\n[patient] no, just the ibuprofen.\n[doctor] okay. and any allergies to medications?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. do you have your medical history record?\n[patient] yes, here you go.\n[doctor] thank you. so, you have anxiety. okay. and any surgeries? you have a lumbar fusion. okay. let\'s take a look at your back. i\'m going to check your range of motion. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] okay, great. i\'m gon na move your back around a little bit. does that hurt?\n[patient] no, not really.\n[doctor] okay. and when i press here?\n[patient] a little bit.\n[doctor] okay. and when i press here?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. when i press here?\n[patient] yes.\n[doctor] okay. i\'m gon na lift your leg up. does that hurt?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. and when i lift it up?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. great. and when i lift it up like this?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. great. and when i lift it up like this?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. great. and when i lift it up like that?\n[patient] no.\n[doctor] okay. great. okay. let\'s check your sensation. can you feel this?\n[patient] yes.\n[doctor] okay. and this?\n[patient] yes.\n[doctor] okay. and this?\n[patient] yes.\n[doctor] okay. great. everything seems to be intact. so, i\'m gon na go ahead and order an x-ray of your back. we\'ll review those results later.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] hey dragon, show me the lumbar x-ray. okay. so, looking at your x-ray, i don\'t see any obvious signs of a fracture, which is good. i can see your prior lumbar fusion and the hardware is in good position.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] so, my impression is that you have a lumbar strain. so, i\'m gon na recommend you continue taking ibuprofen. i\'m gon na prescribe motrin 800 milligrams, three times a day with food. and i\'m gon na recommend using ice and heat. if you\'re in a lot of pain, use ice, and then switch to heat. and if you need to follow up with me, please do.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] any questions?\n[patient] no, that\'s it.\n[doctor] okay. great. thanks, dragon. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi, ms. lee. how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing okay. how are you?\n[doctor] i\'m doing well, thank you. so i see here that you\'re here for an evaluation of back pain. tell me a little bit about what happened.\n[patient] i was at a birthday party and i was running down the stairs and i ran into the railing and twisted my back.\n[doctor] okay. and where is your pain located?\n[patient] it\'s in my lower back.\n[doctor] okay. and does it radiate down