, but wants to make sure that her high blood sugar is not an issue.\n\nThe patient denies any fever or chills. She denies chest pain or shortness of breath. She denies abdominal pain or burning when she urinates. She denies joint pain or muscle aches.\n\nShe notes that she has osteoarthritis, and that nothing seems out of the ordinary for her joint pain.\n\nThe patient has a history of atrial fibrillation. She states that she has felt her heart racing when she is anxious; however, other than that, she has not experienced any issues. She is currently taking metoprolol 25 mg 2 times per day.\n\nRegarding her acid reflux, she states that she has been doing well. She has been taking the medication that was prescribed to her, and it has been very helpful. She is on the Protonix 40 mg once daily, and she is doing well with that\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\n• Constitutional: Negative for fever, chills\n• Cardiovascular: Negative for chest pain\n• Respiratory: Negative for shortness of breath.\n• Gastrointestinal: Negative for abdominal pain.\n• Genitourinary: No dysuria.\n• Musculoskeletal: No Arthralgias, Myalgias.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAMINATION\n\nConstitutional\n• General Appearance: appear in no distress.\n\nNeck\n• General Examination: Her thyroid is a little enlarged but nontender. There are no carotid bruits. Respiratory\n• Auscultation of Lungs: Clear bilaterally. Cardiovascular\n• Auscultation of Heart: Irregular rate and rhythm. Musculoskeletal\n• Examination of Abdomen: Nice soft and have no edema in lower extremities.\n\nRESULTS\n\nGlucose: elevated.\nHbA1c: elevated.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN\n\nMs. Hannah Phillips is a 52-year-old female who presents for evaluation of high blood sugar.\n\nDiabetes.\n• Medical Reasoning: Elevated blood glucose and hemoglobin A1c levels based on recent labs.\n• Additional Testing: We will order a complete metabolic panel for further evaluation.\n• Medical Treatment: Initiate metformin 500 mg twice daily. Encouraged dietary modifications. The patient will be given a glucometer to monitor her glucose levels at home.\n\nAtrial Fibrillation.\n\n• Medical Reasoning: Asymptomatic and well-controlled at this time.\n• Medical Treatment: Continue metoprolol 25 mg twice daily. Refilled today.\n\nHistory of Reflux.\n\n• Medical Reasoning: Well-controlled on current regimen.\n• Medical Treatment: Continue Protonix 40 mg daily.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] hi hannah good to see you today so i know your your notes say that you\'re here for your high blood sugar how are you doing\n[patient] i\'m doing okay i\'ve been eating more sweets during the holidays and i had a really rough week this past week i was really lightheaded i was seeing spots in my vision and i was really dizzy i went to the er and they said my blood sugar was really high they gave me iv fluids and told me to get into a routine and watch my diet but i\'m staying with my family during the holidays and i\'m having trouble getting back into my diet\n[doctor] okay well let\'s go ahead and talk a little bit more about that first i know you said that you went to the er and they found that your blood sugar was high can you tell me a little bit more about that\n[patient] yeah so i was just sitting on the couch watching tv and i just felt really lightheaded and then i started seeing spots and then i felt really dizzy i could barely get up and get to the bathroom i thought i was going to pass out\n[doctor] okay and did you have any fever or chills with that\n[patient] no fever or chills\n[doctor] any chest pain or shortness of breath\n[patient] no chest pain or shortness of breath\n[doctor] any abdominal pain or burning when you urinate\n[patient] no abdominal pain or burning when i urinate\n[doctor] any joint pain or muscle aches\n[patient] i have osteoarthritis and nothing seems out of the ordinary for my joint pain\n[doctor] okay well i know that you have a history of atrial fibrillation how have you been doing with that have you been feeling your heart racing or anything\n[patient] i have felt my heart racing when i\'m anxious but other than that i have not experienced any issues\n[doctor] okay and what medication are you taking for that\n[patient] i\'m taking metoprolol twenty five milligrams twice a day\n[doctor] okay and how are you doing with your acid reflux have you been doing well with that\n[patient] yes i\'ve been doing well i\'ve been taking the medication that was prescribed to me and it has been very helpful i\'m on protonix forty milligrams once daily and i\'m doing well with that\n[doctor] okay well i\'m gon na go ahead and do a quick physical exam on you and then we\'ll talk a little bit more about my assessment and plan okay\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] so on your physical exam you appear in no distress your thyroid is a little bit enlarged but nontender there are no carotid bruits your lungs are clear bilaterally and your heart is irregular rate and rhythm and your abdomen is nice and soft and you have no edema in your lower extremities so let\'s talk a little bit about my assessment and plan for you so first of all i\'m gon na go ahead and order a complete metabolic panel for further evaluation and i\'m gon na go ahead and initiate metformin five hundred milligrams twice a day i want you to start watching your diet as well i\'m gon na give you a glucometer and i want you to check your glucose levels at home okay\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] for your atrial fibrillation i want you to continue the metoprolol twenty five milligrams twice a day and i\'m gon na go ahead and refill that for you and then for your reflux i want you to continue the protonix forty milligrams daily and i\'m gon na go ahead and refill that for you as well so do you have any questions for me\n[patient] no i don\'t think so\n[doctor] okay great well i\'m glad to see you today and i\'m gon na see you