 weeks for blood pressure check and basic metabolic panel. Reduce sodium intake to 1500 to <2000 mg per day. Follow DASH diet.\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] hey jordan, how are you?\n[patient] hey, i\'m good. how are you?\n[doctor] i\'m good. so, jordan, i know the nurse told you about dax. i\'d like to tell dax a little bit about you. so, jordan is a 49-year-old male with a long history of hypertension, but he had an acute episode of palpitations in march, and he went to the er for that, and he\'s here for a follow-up on that.\n[patient] mm-hmm.\n[doctor] so, jordan, tell me about what happened in march. what happened in march?\n[patient] i went to the er because i was having some palpitations and high blood pressure. i thought it was a panic attack at first because i had a lot of anxiety and, uh, i was really worried. but then i thought about it, and i had had several cups of coffee that morning on an empty stomach, and i thought that might have been the cause.\n[doctor] okay. so you think the coffee was the cause of your palpitations?\n[patient] yeah, i do.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any episodes of palpitations since march?\n[patient] no, not since march.\n[doctor] okay. and how have you been monitoring your blood pressure at home?\n[patient] i\'ve been checking it every day, and it\'s been running between 146 and 155.\n[doctor] okay. and are you taking any medications for your blood pressure?\n[patient] yeah, my new primary care doctor put me on benicar hct, and i\'ve been taking that for about a month.\n[doctor] okay. and are you taking any other medications?\n[patient] no, that\'s it.\n[doctor] okay. and how about salt intake? are you watching that?\n[patient] yes, i am. i\'ve been really good about that.\n[doctor] okay. and how about exercise? are you exercising regularly?\n[patient] i do walk on my treadmill as often as i can.\n[doctor] okay. great. and any family history of hypertension?\n[patient] yeah, several fa