at you recently learned that your partner of three years has been engaging in sexual encounters with other people. is that correct?\n[patient] yeah. i found out recently.\n[doctor] okay. and you want to be evaluated for all sexually transmitted diseases?\n[patient] yes, i do.\n[doctor] okay. have you had any abnormal pap smears in the past?\n[patient] i had an abnormal pap smear around the age of 20, but all my pap smears since then, including the one about six months ago, were normal.\n[doctor] okay. thank you. let\'s go ahead and do a physical exam. i\'m just gon na take a look at you. i\'m gon na be as gentle as i can. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] alright. your external genitalia look normal. no external lesions. normal labia majora and labia minora. normal physiological discharge with normal color and odor. i\'m gon na check your cervix. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] your cervix looks normal. your vaginal wall is normal. no cervical motion tenderness or masses noted. i\'m gon na go ahead and swab for the std testing. we\'ll be checking for gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, syphilis, hiv, and hepatitis c. i\'ll call you with the results of the laboratory testing. do you have any questions?\n[patient] no, that\'s it.\n[doctor] okay. thank you. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi, ms. ross. how are you?\n[patient] i\'m okay, doctor. how are you?\n[doctor] i\'m doing well. thank you. so, you\'re here for full-spectrum std testing. i see that you\'re 23 years old, so that\'s a great time to come in and get checked out.\n[patient] yeah, i\'m just trying to be safe.\n[doctor] yeah, absolutely. i mean, we\'ve seen a lot of stds lately, and it\'s just important to stay on top of things.\n[patient] yeah, definitely.\n[doctor] so, what are you experiencing?\n[patient] i\'ve been having some discomfort, and there\'s a change in my discharge and odor down there. and the right side of my vagina is starting to become painful.\n[doctor] okay. and do you ha