STRUCTIONS\n\nCall the clinic if symptoms worsen. The patient will have a follow-up appointment in 4 weeks.\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] hi, jacqueline. how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing well. how are you?\n[doctor] i\'m doing well. i\'m sorry i\'m a little early. i know you said you wanted to come in at 8:00.\n[patient] yes, i did.\n[doctor] so, jacqueline, i know you were here last time for perioral dermatitis. how are you doing with that?\n[patient] i\'m doing okay. it\'s not fully resolved, but it\'s much better.\n[doctor] okay. and i know you were using the doxycycline twice a day. how are you doing with that?\n[patient] i was doing that for a little while, but my pharmacist said, you know, she said, " hey, you can cut that down to once a day. it\'s working."\n[doctor] okay. and so you\'ve been doing that for a week now?\n[patient] yeah, for about a week.\n[doctor] okay. and has it improved?\n[patient] it hasn\'t gotten worse, but it\'s not fully resolved.\n[doctor] okay. have you noticed any drying of the skin?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t noticed any drying of the skin.\n[doctor] okay. and you\'re still using the sulfacetamide wash twice a day?\n[patient] yes, i am.\n[doctor] okay. and are you applying the metrocream right after the sulfacetamide wash?\n[patient] yes, i am.\n[doctor] okay. and are you using any other lotions or products?\n[patient] no, i\'m not.\n[doctor] okay. i know you were thinking about the elidel, but you were concerned about the side effects. have you decided to use that at all?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t. i\'m just worried about the side effects.\n[doctor] okay. well, we\'ll talk a little bit more about that in a second. so, let\'s do a quick physical exam. i\'m just gon na look at your skin on your face. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] on your bilateral medial cheeks, i do see a few very faint erythematous papules with some mild redness around and underneath the nostrils. how have you been doing with your rosacea?\n[patient] i\'ve been doing okay with that.\n[doctor] okay. and you\'re using the metrocream twice a day for that?\n[patient] yes, i am.\n[doctor] okay. and are you washing your eyelids gently with a cleanser?\n[patient] yes, i am.\n[doctor] okay. and are you using any other creams on your eyelids?\n[patient] no, just the metrocream.\n[doctor] okay. well, let me tell you a little bit about my assessment and plan. so, for your perioral dermatitis, i think you need to go back to using the doxycycline twice a day until we reach full resolution, and then you can go back to once a day for an additional week. i know your pharmacist said you could go to once a day, but i think we need to push through a little bit longer to get it fully resolved. how does that sound to you?\n[patient] that sounds good to me.\n[doctor] okay. and i don\'t think you should be using the elidel. i know you were concerned about the side effects, but i don\'t think it\'s necessary at this time. i would like to prescribe tacrolimus ointment. it\'s a very potent cream. you can apply a thin layer to the affected area twice a day. it\'s very expensive, but i think it will really help. are you okay with that?\n[patient] yes, i\'m okay with that.\n[doctor] okay. and continue using the sulfacetamide wash once a day, and use the bruder mask as needed. and for your rosacea, continue using the metrocream twice daily. i would also recommend washing your eyelids gently with a cleanser once daily and trying a gentle cream such as vanicream. do you have any questions?\n[patient] no, i don\'t.\n[doctor] okay. great. and we\'ll see you back in four weeks. if your symptoms worsen, please call the clinic.\n[patient] okay, i will.\n[doctor] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi jacqueline good to see you today\n[patient] good to see you too\n[doctor] so i know that you have a history of perioral dermatitis and rosacea including ocular rosacea so how are you doing with your perioral dermatitis\n[patient] it\'s well controlled but it\'s not gone away completely\n[doctor] okay so you were using the doxycycline twice a day\n[patient] i was but my pharmacist said i could cut back to once a day since it was improving so i\'ve been doing that for about a week now\n[doctor] okay and has it continued to improve or has it worsened at all\n[patient] it\'s not gotten any better but it\'s not gotten any worse\n[doctor] okay\n[patient] and i\'m still using the sulfacetamide wash twice a day and it\'s really helped my skin is much improved moisturization\n[doctor] okay and you\'re using the metrocream after the sulfacetamide wash\n[patient] yes i am\n[doctor] okay and have you tried any other lotions or creams or anything like that\n[patient] no i\'ven\'t i\'ve been trying to stay away from that\n[doctor] okay and what about the cetaphil lotion or soap or the neutrogena wipes\n[patient] no i haven\'t tried any of those\n[doctor] okay and i know you were thinking about using elidel\n[patient] yeah i was but it\'s not covered by my insurance and i was worried about some of the side effects\n[doctor] okay\n[patient] so i decided to pass on that\n[doctor] okay alright so let\'s take a look at your skin now i know you\'ve been using the sulfacetamide wash and the metrocream so let\'s take a look at your skin now\n[doctor] okay so i\'m just gon na do a quick skin inspection of your face and i do see on your bilateral medial cheeks a few very faint erythematous papules with some mild redness around and underneath the nostrils and your fitzpatrick skin type is a four to five\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] so let\'s talk a little bit about your perioral dermatitis so it\'s improved but it has not resolved so i\'m gon na recommend that you go back to using the doxycycline twice a day and i know you\'ve been using it once a day and it has improved but it\'s not fully resolved so let\'s go back to twice a day and then once it\'s fully resolved you can reduce it to once a day