STRUCTIONS\n\nCall the clinic if symptoms worsen. The patient will have a follow-up appointment in 4 weeks.\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] hi, jacqueline. how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing well. how are you?\n[doctor] i\'m doing well. i\'m sorry i\'m a little early. i know you said you wanted to come in at 8:00.\n[patient] yes, i did.\n[doctor] so, jacqueline, i know you were here last time for perioral dermatitis. how are you doing with that?\n[patient] i\'m doing okay. it\'s not fully resolved, but it\'s much better.\n[doctor] okay. and i know you were using the doxycycline twice a day. how are you doing with that?\n[patient] i was doing that for a little while, but my pharmacist said, you know, she said, " hey, you can cut that down to once a day. it\'s working."\n[doctor] okay. and so you\'ve been doing that for a week now?\n[patient] yeah, for about a week.\n[doctor] okay. and has it improved?\n[patient] it hasn\'t gotten worse, but it\'s not fully resolved.\n[doctor] okay. have you noticed any drying of the skin?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t noticed any drying of the skin.\n[doctor] okay. and you\'re still using the sulfacetamide wash twice a day?\n[patient] yes, i am.\n[doctor] okay. and are you applying the metrocream right after the sulfacetamide wash?\n[patient] yes, i am.\n[doctor] okay. and are you using any other lotions or products?\n[patient] no, i\'m not.\n[doctor] okay. i know you were thinking about the elidel, but you were concerned about the side effects. have you decided to use that at all?\n[patient] no, i haven\'t. i\'m just worried about the side effects.\n[doctor] okay. well, we\'ll talk a little bit more about that in a second. so, let\'s do a quick physical exam. i\'m just gon na look at your skin on your face. okay?\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] on your bilateral medial cheeks, i do see a few very faint erythematous papules with some mild redness around and underneath the nostrils. how have you been doing with 