ackle football.\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] hi, matthew. how are you?\n[patient] hey, i\'m good. how are you?\n[doctor] i\'m good. so i see you\'re here for your right shoulder. what happened?\n[patient] yeah, so i was playing a little pickup football, and i got tackled a couple of times and landed on my right shoulder.\n[doctor] okay. and how long ago did that happen?\n[patient] that was four days ago.\n[doctor] okay. and did you continue playing?\n[patient] i did. i was able to get back in the game.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any pain since then?\n[patient] yeah, i\'ve had pain since then.\n[doctor] okay. where is the pain located?\n[patient] it\'s the back of my shoulder.\n[doctor] okay. do you have any numbness or tingling in your fingers?\n[patient] no, no numbness or tingling.\n[doctor] okay. and is the strength in your hand okay?\n[patient] the strength in my hand is okay, but i\'ve been trying to avoid lifting anything too heavy.\n[doctor] okay. and can you touch your shoulder to your ear?\n[patient] no, i can\'t touch my ear.\n[doctor] okay. have you taken anything for the pain?\n[patient] yeah, i\'ve been taking tylenol, but it doesn\'t really help.\n[doctor] okay. have you had any neck problems or other joint problems?\n[patient] no, no neck problems or other joint problems.\n[doctor] any previous injuries to your right shoulder?\n[patient] no, no previous injuries to my right shoulder.\n[doctor] any fever or chills since the injury?\n[patient] no, no fever or chills, but i have had a headache.\n[doctor] okay. did you hit your head at the time of the injury?\n[patient] i hit my head, but i didn\'t pass out.\n[doctor] okay. and how is your headache?\n[patient] it\'s not too bad.\n[doctor] okay. let\'s go ahead and take a look at your vitals. your blood pressure is 122 over 76. your heart rate is 82. your oxygen saturation is 95 percent on room air. let\'s go ahead and do a physical exam. i\'m gon na start with your neck. does that hurt?\n[patient] no, it doesn\'t hurt.\n[doctor] okay. and your head, there doesn\'t appear to be any trauma. there\'s no ecchymosis or bruising. let\'s move on to your shoulder. i\'m going to palpate your right shoulder. does this hurt?\n[patient] yes, that hurts.\n[doctor] okay. i\'m gon na go ahead and move your arm. can you move your arm for me?\n[patient] yeah, but it hurts.\n[doctor] okay. you do have pain with abduction and adduction to about 90 degrees only. does it hurt when i rotate your arm like this?\n[patient] yes, that hurts.\n[doctor] okay. i can appreciate your radial artery pulse. let\'s look at your x-ray. okay, so your x-ray shows an acute fracture of the acromioclavicular joint. i\'m going to order a ct of your right shoulder to further evaluate that. i\'m gon na go ahead and order a ct of your right shoulder to further evaluate that. i\'m going to place you in a sling and prescribe meloxicam 15 milligrams once a day for the pain. i\'m also going to recommend formal physical therapy to strengthen your right shoulder in hopes of avoiding surgery in the future. in the meantime, i do recommend that you avoid tackle football.\n[patient] okay.\n[doctor] do you have any questions?\n[patient] no, that sounds good.\n[doctor] okay, well, i\'ll see you back in a couple of weeks to check on your progress. take care.\n[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hey, matthew, how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing okay, i guess.\n[doctor] good to see you. so, i know the nurse told you about dax. i\'m dax. i\'m your physician today. so, i know the nurse told you about dax. i\'m looking at your information here and i see that you\'re a right-hand dominant athlete. you play football, so, i\'m a big football fan. i\'m a dallas cowboys fan. how about you? who do you like?\n[patient] i like the patriots.\n[doctor] oh, okay. so, i\'m a big dallas cowboys fan, so, i\'m glad you like the patriots. so, tell me, what happened?\n[patient