n having pain in my right knee for about 2.5 weeks now. it started when i stepped off a curb and turned over my ankle.\n[doctor] okay. and where in your knee is the pain located?\n[patient] it\'s on the outside of my knee.\n[doctor] okay. and does the pain go away with time?\n[patient] it doesn\'t really go away, but it doesn\'t get any worse.\n[doctor] okay. and is the pain constant or does it come and go?\n[patient] it\'s pretty constant.\n[doctor] okay. and does anything make the pain better or worse?\n[patient] standing on one foot for a long time makes it hurt. standing for a long time makes it hurt.\n[doctor] okay. and does it hurt when you\'re resting or when you\'re moving around?\n[patient] it doesn\'t hurt when i\'m resting or when i\'m moving around. it hurts when i\'m standing on my heel.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any numbness or tingling in your foot?\n[patient] yes, i do. that\'s not new.\n[doctor] okay. and have you been doing anything to try to relieve the pain?\n[patient] i\'ve been taking ibuprofen, which helps at night. i\'ve also been icing my knee four times a day, and that helps in the morning and at the end of the day.\n[doctor] okay. and how active are you during the day?\n[patient] i\'m more active during the day, but that doesn\'t really impact my knee pain.\n[doctor] okay. and are you able to perform a full squat without pain?\n[patient] yes, i can do a full squat without pain.\n[doctor] okay. and have you had any previous injuries to this knee?\n[patient] no, this is the first time.\n[doctor] okay. and do you have any pain with walking?\n[patient] no, not really. just standing on one foot for a long time.\n[doctor] okay. and any pain when you\'re sitting or laying down?\n[patient] no, not really.\n[doctor] okay. and any pain when your foot is flat on the ground?\n[patient] no, not really.\n[doctor] okay. and how about locking of the knee, does that happen with prolonged standing?\n[patient] yes, it does.\n[doctor] okay. and any pain