ead and do a varus test on your knee. i\'m gon na push down on your knee. does that hurt?\n[patient] no, it doesn\'t hurt.\n[doctor] okay. and i\'m gon na go ahead and do a lachman\'s test. i\'m gon na pull your foot out from under you. does that hurt?\n[patient] no, it doesn\'t hurt.\n[doctor] okay. and i\'m gon na check your range of motion. i\'m gon na bend your knee. okay. i\'m gon na straighten it out. okay. i\'m gon na bend it the other way. okay. can you do that on your own?\n[patient] yes, i can.\n[doctor] okay. great. i\'m gon na go ahead and check your pulses. i\'m gon na feel your dorsalis pedis and posterior tibialis pulses. okay, you have a palpable dorsalis pedis and posterior tibialis pulse. i\'m gon na go ahead and look at your knee. i see a little bit of swelling and a little bit of effusion. there\'s no pain with palpation of your right lateral knee. you do have a positive varus test. you have a full range of motion. you have a negative lachman\'s test. i\'m gon na go ahead and look at your x-rays. hey, dragon, show me the first view. okay, your x-rays look good. i don\'t see any fractures or dislocations. i don\'t see any bony abnormalities. i\'m gon na go ahead and order a few more views. hey, dragon, show me the next view. okay, that looks good. i don\'t see any fractures or dislocations. i don\'t see any bony abnormalities. i\'m gon na go ahead and order one more view. hey, dragon, show me the next view. okay, that looks good. i don\'t see any fractures or dislocations. i don\'t see any bony abnormalities. so, greg, based on your exam and your x-rays, it looks like you have a right knee lateral collateral ligament strain. i\'m gon na go ahead and recommend that we treat you conservatively with formal physical therapy to strengthen your right knee. i\'m gon na prescribe you meloxicam 15 mg to treat your pain. if your pain doesn\'t improve with physical therapy, i\'m gon na recommend obtaining an mri. do you have any questions for me?\n[patient] 