t] yes that\'s fine\n[doctor] okay and i\'m gon na recommend that we put you in a surgical shoe to provide increased support i\'m also gon na prescribe you collagenase ointment to apply to your wound one time per day and cover it with a sterile dressing and this should be continued until we see the ulcer decrease in size and i want you to follow up with me in two weeks to check on your progress and i\'m gon na put an order for an ankle brachial index to assess the blood flow to your foot and an x-ray of your right foot to rule out osteomyelitis and we\'ll be back in two weeks to see how you\'re doing with that sounds good\n[patient] okay that sounds good\n[doctor] okay thank you\n[patient] thank you\n[doctor] you\'re welcome }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi christina how are you\n[patient] i\'m doing okay i i i\'m just a little tired today\n[doctor] yeah i know it\'s been a long day i\'m glad you were able to make it in today i know you\'ve been having some problems with your foot i i i just wanted to take a look at it so christina what seems to be the problem with your foot\n[patient] well it\'s this ulcer on my right foot it\'s been there for a year now and it just seems to be getting worse\n[doctor] okay and how did this start\n[patient] well it started as a blister and i picked at it and it turned red\n[doctor] okay and did you see a doctor for that\n[patient] yeah i did i saw my primary care doctor and she put me on keflex and that helped a little bit but it didn\'t go away\n[doctor] okay and when was the last time you took keflex\n[patient] about five months ago\n[doctor] okay and do you have any pain with it\n[patient] no i don\'t have any pain but i do have decreased sensation in my foot and it\'s been draining a lot more\n[doctor] okay and have you been wearing your regular shoes\n[patient] yeah i have been\n[doctor] okay okay and i know you have type two diabetes and neuropathy how are your sugars running\n[patient] they\'re running a little 