] okay and when i tap on the inside of your wrist here does that cause any tingling or pain\n[patient] yeah that\'s tingling\n[doctor] okay that\'s a positive tinsel\'s sign alright so i\'m gon na order an emg nerve conduction study of your right hand and wrist to further evaluate your symptoms and i\'m gon na go ahead and order an x-ray of your right hand and wrist as well to rule out any bony abnormalities now based on your symptoms and your exam it sounds like you have carpal tunnel syndrome so let\'s talk a little bit about what that is and what we can do to treat it carpal tunnel syndrome is a condition where the median nerve that runs through your wrist is compressed at the wrist and can cause pain numbness and tingling in the thumb and the first three fingers of the hand and this is often caused by repetitive movements such as typing or using a mouse and it can be quite painful and it can interfere with your daily activities so for treatment of this i would like you to continue taking the ibuprofen but i would like to increase the dose to six hundred milligrams four times a day and i\'m also gon na recommend that you wear a wrist splint at night and this will help to alleviate some of the symptoms and i\'m gon na also order that emg nerve conduction study to further evaluate your symptoms and if the study is positive we can consider additional treatment with physical therapy or even surgical intervention with a carpal tunnel release so do you have any questions about that\n[patient] no that sounds good\n[doctor] okay alright so we will get that ordered for you and i\'ll see you back in about four weeks to check on your progress\n[patient] okay sounds good thank you\n[doctor] you\'re welcome }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hey alexis good to see you today how are you doing\n[patient] i\'m doing okay i\'m here for my right hand pain\n[doctor] okay so i see here in my notes that you\'ve been having some right hand pain for about six months now\n[pati