i try to move my arm\n[doctor] okay have you noticed any swelling or bruising\n[patient] yeah there\'s a little bit of swelling and bruising\n[doctor] okay and have you taken any medication for it\n[patient] i took some ibuprofen but it didn\'t really help\n[doctor] okay and have you tried ice or any of that\n[patient] i iced it a little bit but not too much\n[doctor] okay and how about any other symptoms like chest pain or abdominal pain\n[patient] no no chest pain or anything like that\n[doctor] okay good and how about any numbness or tingling in your fingers\n[patient] no\n[doctor] okay and can you move your elbow for me\n[patient] yeah i can move it but it hurts\n[doctor] okay and how about flexion and extension is that painful\n[patient] yeah it hurts a little bit\n[doctor] okay and is it painful when i push here on the back of your elbow\n[patient] yeah that hurts\n[doctor] okay and do you have any other medical conditions\n[patient] yeah i have high blood pressure and diabetes\n[doctor] okay and are those both well controlled\n[patient] yeah i think so\n[doctor] okay and are you taking any medications for those\n[patient] yeah i\'m taking lisinopri for my blood pressure and metformin for my diabetes\n[doctor] okay and how\'s your blood pressure been\n[patient] it\'s been good\n[doctor] okay and your blood pressure today is one fifty over ninety which is a little high but not too bad how about your blood sugar\n[patient] it\'s been good\n[doctor] okay and have you had any recent labs done\n[patient] i had an a1c done about two weeks ago and it was pretty good\n[doctor] okay good so let\'s talk a little bit about your diet how\'s that going\n[patient] i\'ve been trying to watch what i eat\n[doctor] okay good and how about exercise\n[patient] i play lacrosse\n[doctor] okay and when you say lacrosse are you playing goalie or\n[patient] i\'m a midfielder\n[doctor] okay so you\'re running around a lot\n[patient] yeah\n[doctor] okay and do you play with any other sports\n[patient] yeah i also play soccer\n[doctor] okay and how often do you play lacrosse\n[patient] about two to three times a week\n[doctor] okay and how often do you play soccer\n[patient] about the same\n[doctor] okay and have you had any injuries with those sports\n[patient] just this elbow\n[doctor] okay and let\'s take a look at your x-ray here your x-ray of your elbow looks good there\'s no evidence of a fracture or any bony abnormalities so that\'s good so let\'s go ahead and i\'m gon na do a quick physical exam on you so your heart sounds are normal and your lungs are clear so i\'m gon na go ahead and examine your elbow so i\'m gon na press here on the back of your elbow does that hurt\n[patient] yeah that hurts\n[doctor] okay and i\'m gon na move your elbow up and down does that hurt\n[patient] yeah a little bit\n[doctor] okay so you do have some pain with that motion but otherwise normal range of motion there is some swelling and bruising as well as some ecchymosis so i think you have a contusion of your elbow so i\'m gon na go ahead and order a new x-ray just to make sure there\'s nothing else going on but i don\'t think there\'s a fracture so for your first problem i\'m gon na recommend that you avoid playing lacrosse for the next couple of weeks just until your elbow heals after that you should be fine to continue playing normally i\'m also gon na prescribe you some ibuprofen eight hundred milligrams twice daily to help with some of the pain and swelling and you should also ice the area in twenty minute intervals three times a day to further reduce your symptoms for your hypertension i\'m gon na keep you on your lisinopril twenty milligrams daily and for your diabetes i\'m gon na keep you on the metformin five hundred milligrams and i\'m gon na order an a1c to evaluate any need for medication adjustments do you have any questions for me\n[patient] no\n[doctor] okay great thanks for coming in\n[patient] thank you }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ [doctor] hi, dave, how are you?\n[patient] i\'m doing alright.\n[doctor] good. so i know that you\'ve had some elbow pain, so let\'s talk about that first. so you\'re here for right elbow pain.\n[patient] yeah, so i was playing lacrosse over the weekend and my son hit me with a lacrosse stick and i\'ve been having some pain since.\n[doctor] okay. and how would you rate that pain?\n[patient] probably like a seven out of ten.\n[doctor] okay. and is it more when you move it or when you just have it still?\n[patient] it\'s more when i move it.\n[doctor] okay. and are you having any numbness or tingling in that hand or fingers?\n[patient] no, nothing like that.\n[doctor] okay. and any swelling?\n[patient] a little bit.\n[doctor] okay. and bruising?\n[patient] yeah, there\'s a little bruising.\n[doctor] okay. so let\'s go ahead and look at your vitals. so your blood pressure is a little high, 150 over 90, but we\'ve seen that before, so that\'s okay. so let\'s go ahead and do a quick physical exam. so i\'m just gon na listen to your heart and lungs real quick. so on your heart exam, i do appreciate a two out of six systolic ejection murmur, which is the same as last time. and on your lung exam, your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. so i\'m just gon na do a quick exam of your elbow. so i\'m gon na push on it a little bit. does that hurt?\n[patient] yeah, it hurts.\n[doctor] okay. so i\'m gon na move it a little bit. so there is some swelling about the elbow and there is some ecchymosis. so i\'m gon na look at some results. so we did an x-ray of your right elbow and it does not show any evidence of a fracture or any bony abnormalities. so what i think you have is a contusion of your elbow, and i think that you got hit with that lacrosse stick. so i\'m gon na prescribe you some ibuprofen, eight hundred milligrams, twice a day, and you can ice it for twenty minutes at a time, three times a day. that should help with the pain and the swelling. and i want you to take a couple of weeks off of lacrosse, just till it heals, and then you can go back and play normally. so does that sound good to you?\n[patient] yeah, that sounds fine.\n[doctor] okay. and i know that you have hypertension, and that seems to be well controlled with your diet and your lisinopril. so i\'m just gon na keep you on the lisinopril twenty milligrams a day, and just keep up with your diet. and i know you have diabetes, and that also seems to be well controlled. i\'m gon na keep you on the metformin five hundred milligrams, and i\'m gon na order a hemoglobin a1c to make sure that we don\'t need to make any adjustments to your diabetes medications. does that all sound good to you?\n[patient] yeah, that sounds fine.\n[doctor] okay. and i know that you have some bruising on your elbow, and i\'m just gon na go ahead and examine that. so on your hematologic exam, i do see some bruising on your right elbow. alright, so i think we have a good plan. do you have any questions for me?\n[patient] no, i don\'t think so.\n[doctor] okay. all right, so i\'ll see you back in a couple of weeks. take care.\n[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Reference Answer:\n[doctor] hey good to see you philip so i see here you\'re coming in you had some right elbow pain also you have a past medical history of hypertension diabetes we are gon na check up on those as well so can you tell me what happened to your elbow\n[patient] sure i hurt it about a week ago playing lacrosse with my kids just suddenly started hurting me when i was throwing the ball\n[doctor] okay okay so how old are your kids\n[patient] my oldest is thirteen and the other one is ten i was playing with a thirteen -year-old\n[doctor] okay yeah i know i i play with my kids sometimes and i think i\'m getting too old to do all that so i just i\'ve hurt myself before as well alright so with your your elbow what part of your elbow would you say hurts\n[patient] it\'s really like right at the point of the elbow right at right at like the tip of it\n[doctor] okay\n[patient] and it just it hurt hurts anytime i move it\n[doctor] anytime i move it do you remember falling\n[patient] no i do n\'t think so but my kid got pretty rough with me and was checking me several times with a sick\n[doctor] okay\n[patient] so i could have got hit there\n[doctor] okay alright yeah that that that definitely makes sense so how would you describe the pain is it like a dull pain is it stabbing what what would you say\n[patient] it it\'s a pretty sharp pain\n[doctor] okay\n[patient] anytime i move\n[doctor] okay and does it radiate down your arm or does it stay in that one spot\n[patient] it radiates down the forearm\n[doctor] radiates down the forearm alright so have you taken any medications for it to make it better\n[patient] i tried taking advil couple of days but i usually just forget about it\n[doctor] okay when you took it did it did it help at all did it change your your pain score\n[patient] yeah i i think it helped some\n[doctor] okay that\'s good alright so we\'ll we\'ll do a physical exam on that elbow we\'ll take a look at it in a second but i do wan na talk to you about your your hypertension you came in today i know you have past medical history of hypertension came in today your blood pressure\'s a little bit high it was a one fifty over seven over ninety which is pretty high today i see you\'re on twenty of lisinopril have you been taking that daily\n[patient] yes\n[doctor] okay so maybe you just have a little little white coat syndrome i know i have that myself and even though i\'m a physician i i still do n\'t like to go to the doctor so i definitely understand how about your diet i know we talked a little bit about that before and you said kinda during the pandemic you fell off a little bit how you been doing that have you been lowering your salt intake\n[patient] yeah but i only eat low salt items avoid adding salt to food kind of the whole whole family follows like a you know like a mediterranean diet\n[doctor] okay\n[patient] we try to be pretty good about it\n[doctor] okay yeah that\'s good that that\'s that\'s definitely good yeah i know a lot of people during the pandemic it was you know sitting at home and and eating more than we should but that\'s i\'m very happy that you\'ve been compliant and you have that low salt diet so let\'s talk about your diabetes i think you see here on on five hundred of metformin are you taking that as well daily\n[patient] yes\n[doctor] okay and your blood sugars how have they been\n[patient] since i do n\'t take insulin i do n\'t check it everyday when i have checked it it\'s usually running somewhere between eighty to a hundred\n[doctor] okay yeah that\'s that\'s really good yeah so i that\'s that\'s pretty good so what we\'re gon na do we\'re gon na get a a1c just to see you know that range and it\'s possibility we can we can you know lower that metformin dosage but we will do that after your visit then we will take a look at that so lem me go ahead and will do that quick exam of your elbow but first i want to make sure you\'re not having any chest pain or anything like that\n[patient] no\n[doctor] no belly pain\n[patient] no\n[doctor] alright so listen to your lungs so your lungs are clear bilaterally listen to your heart so your heart exam you do still have that grade two out of six systolic ejection murmur but we know it about that before so let me take a look at your elbow so when i press right here on the back of your elbow is that painful\n[patient] yes\n[doctor] alright so when i have you you you flex and extend it it\'s painful does that does that hurt\n[patient] yes it does\n[doctor] alright so your right elbow exam shows you have pain to palpation of the olecranon area of the posterior elbow you do have mild pain with flexion and extension but you do have also normal range of motion at that elbow so we we did do an x-ray before you came in and luckily nothing\'s broken no fracture no bony abnormality so it