ence of trauma or deformity on your back exam i do see some midline tenderness at the l four to five disc space with right-sided lumbar paravertebral tenderness and pain with lumbar flexion and i do get a positive straight leg test in your left leg so i\'m gon na go ahead and look at your results so your mri of the lumbar spine showed some disc desiccation and a disc bulge with a paracentral disc herniation resulting in moderate right neural foraminal stenosis so what does all of that mean kyle so it means that you have a herniated disc in your back which is causing the pain and the pain is radiating down your left leg and it\'s causing some nerve irritation so i think the best course of treatment is going to be a corticosteroid injection which will help with the inflammation and the pain and it\'s a very safe procedure the risks are bleeding infection nerve damage blood vessel damage reaction to the medication including skin changes swelling and elevated glucose levels if you\'re diabetic so do you have any questions for me\n[patient] no\n[doctor] okay and i\'ll go ahead and call in the nurse and we\'ll get you ready for the injection\n[patient] okay\n[doctor] all right thank you\n[patient] thank you }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Reference Answer:\n[doctor] hey kyle so i see here on your chart that you\'ve been having some back pain could you tell me like how you\'ve been doing what\'s going on\n[patient] yeah i have this real bad low back pain it started a couple of weeks ago i was lifting something and i just felt a pop and i i do n\'t know what\'s going on\n[doctor] okay and so you were like moving what what were you moving exactly when you say lifting\n[patient] i was lifting a box of books\n[doctor] okay\n[patient] yeah\n[doctor] alright did we use proper lifting technique do you wonder\n[patient] you know probably not\n[doctor] okay alright i\'m sorry about that alright can you describe the pain for me\n[patient] yeah i i feel like kind of it\'s like achy and sharp\n[do